  "id": "Compound::DB00187 - Gene::154",
  "verbalization": "Esmolol, a selective beta-blocker, is shown to bind to Adrb1, a subunit of the beta-adrenergic receptor, and this binding is linked to the participation of Adrb1 in Beta-adrenergic Receptor Activity. This activity is further associated with Adrb2, suggesting a potential role in the regulation of adrenergic signaling. Additionally, Esmolol's interaction with Adrb1 is also linked to Norepinephrine Binding, which is similarly associated with Adrb2. These findings collectively imply that Esmolol may influence Adrb2 through a shared pathway involving the beta-adrenergic receptor, possibly by modulating receptor activity or function. The evidence suggests a mechanistic link between Esmolol and Adrb2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
